      "discord_url": null,
      "changelog": "v0.3.0: Pure Lua: the MQTT client runs in Keyglass itself (host network permission), no Python, so it works on any Mac or Windows PC. v0.2.0: Uses the keycap renderer's built-in glow (needs keys-renderer with rule.glow). v0.1.3: The glow is small and centered on the icon instead of filling the key. v0.1.2: Active keys get a soft back glow that fades in and out (and breathes while a press awaits confirmation) instead of an LED dot and border. v0.1.1: Home Assistant entity ids follow the button id (event.<node>_<id>) via default_entity_id. v0.1.0: First release.",
